# UI deploy (frontend → production)

Production UI CD runs only on **{UiRepo}** (`git remote suite-ui`), not on the monorepo `origin`.

CI (`frontend/.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) runs **`npm run lint`** before **`npm run build`**. **ESLint errors fail the pipeline** (warnings don't).

## Before any UI subtree push

```powershell
cd frontend
npm run lint
```

Fix **all errors** first. Optionally run `npm run build` and `npm run build:demo` (CI runs both).

## Commit scope (default)

When the user asks to push/deploy the UI and doesn't name files:

1. `git add` **every** uncommitted change under `frontend/` (not `frontend/.vite/` or other generated caches).
2. One commit covering them.
3. Don't cherry-pick only this chat's files unless told "only these files".

If nothing is uncommitted under `frontend/`, say so; run lint + subtree push only if they still want production updated.

## Release steps

1. Commit under `frontend/`.
2. Lint (mandatory, 0 errors).
3. From repo root:
   ```powershell
   .\backend\scripts\Push-SuiteDeploy.ps1 -Ui
   ```
   Or: `git subtree split --prefix=frontend -b frontend-ui-release` then `git push suite-ui frontend-ui-release:master`.
4. Verify [{UiRepo} Actions](https://github.com/{GitHubOwner}/{UiRepo}/actions): **build** then **deploy** green.
5. `git push origin` alone is not a frontend release.

FTP secrets live on the UI repo; never commit FTP credentials.

## Agent checklist

- Check-in/push/deploy request → commit all `frontend/` changes, lint (fix errors), push `origin` if ahead, run `Push-SuiteDeploy.ps1 -Ui` in the same turn. Don't ask again.
- "Everything up-to-date" on push means **no new Actions run** — only a new commit triggers CD.
